window.LEARN = {"projects":[["badnorth","Bad North 2017–19"],["townscaper","Townscaper 2019–21"],["next","第三项目 2021–25"],["other","其他"]],"topics":[["water","水 / 岸线"],["grid","网格 / 拓扑"],["light","光照 / 阴影"],["terrain","地形 / 岛屿"],["build","建筑 / 模块"],["life","植被 / 生物 / 装饰"],["texture","贴图 / 风格"],["fx","Bad North 玩法 / 特效"],["tools","UI / 工具 / 工程"],["show","展示 / 无技术说明"]],"labels":{"done":"重构版已实现","game":"已用于 Townscaper","engine":"已在 engine 实现","both":"两边都用了","partial":"部分实现","ref":"学习参考","todo":"未实现","na":"与项目无关"},"items":[{"id":"1995813566344011807","date":"2025-12-02","text":"I'm designing a jungle gym / climbable shelf structure for the play area of our home. The sofa-like structure to the left is folding mattress you can slide under the monkey bars. If you've ever build something similar I'd be happy to take advice","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"家里的攀爬架，与游戏无关","project":"other"},{"id":"1991103578011029507","date":"2025-11-19","text":"I think it gives a pretty good sense of a dynamic ocean without being too distractive","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（海面漂移）","note":"动态海面但不抢戏：极低幅度的颜色漂移","project":"next"},{"id":"1991101097818403263","date":"2025-11-19","text":"It's based on a looping vertex shader. The data is baked at generation-time. Each vert has an in-direction, an out-direction and a time offset.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"循环顶点着色器；生成时烘焙：每个顶点存入射点、出射点、时间偏移。讨论串：\"没有整块海面网格\"、\"浪会反弹\"","project":"next"},{"id":"1991099314714902634","date":"2025-11-19","text":"Got some pretty sweet new shore waves going","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"新的岸浪","project":"next"},{"id":"1897266928961700215","date":"2025-03-05","text":"Yet another hallway design","topic":"build","status":"ref","where":"","note":"又一版走廊设计，造型参考","project":"other"},{"id":"1890018647655272491","date":"2025-02-13","text":"Further iterations on hallway design","topic":"build","status":"ref","where":"","note":"走廊设计迭代（家居/建筑设计），作为造型参考","project":"other"},{"id":"1852334860137849222","date":"2024-11-01","text":"A fluffy cloud shader. It is using the same impostors as the trees, in case that isn't obvious.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/impostor.js","note":"同一个烘焙器烘一团白色云团块；实例放大、alpha 用 smoothstep 做软边、底部偏灰、沿风向在着色器里慢慢飘","project":"next"},{"id":"1849732997945110651","date":"2024-10-25","text":"Here, the shoreline is shown in yellow. A pushed out and smoothed shoreline is shown in blue. The waves travel from the blue line to the yellow (and back a little). There is also a global water mask texture that adds extra foam around rocks and stuff.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"黄线=岸线，蓝线=外推并平滑的岸线；浪从蓝走到黄再退回一点","project":"next"},{"id":"1849730611964973481","date":"2024-10-25","text":"Shoreline waves! This is something I've tackled many times. Although this one is very subtle, it's my favorite thus far. Instead of trying to make the waves roll in and out inside one shader pass, I'm creating loads of overlapping waves that each go through their own cycle","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"岸浪：许多重叠的浪各走各的周期","project":"next"},{"id":"1849427564034498642","date":"2024-10-24","text":"Made some octagonal impostors for these trees. Might seem like overkill for such a stylized look, but they're a lot more stable when rotating the camera than all other billboard solutions I've tried, which is kinda important.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/impostor.js","note":"8 个水平方位（每 45°）各烘一张进图集；每棵树一个只绕 Y 轴的四边形，按\"镜头相对这棵树朝向的方位角\"取相邻两张按角度混合 → 转镜头稳定；alpha 边缘一圈墨色","project":"next"},{"id":"1798310423554658732","date":"2024-06-05","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1795831296952041691","date":"2024-05-29","text":"I'm putting together a navigation structure that lets you travel faster along rivers (and especially downstream)","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/world/navgraph.js","note":"河上的边更便宜，顺流最快","project":"next"},{"id":"1791049306213912823","date":"2024-05-16","text":"Trying out a new lighting solution. This one is just one lookup in the vertex shader of a low res cube map height map.","topic":"light","status":"ref","where":"","note":"新光照：顶点着色器里查一次低分辨率立方体高度图。思路记下（和我们的体素阴影是同一类\"查表代替光追\"），没单做","project":"next"},{"id":"1786014232594485497","date":"2024-05-02","text":"Mountain textures! These have been tricky. Mountains kinda need lighting and normals, but with my texture blending tech I don't think I can afford that on low-end devices","topic":"light","status":"ref","where":"","note":"山的贴图：山需要光照和法线，但低端设备负担不起（画面：雪山 + 河）；没做","project":"next"},{"id":"1783792917183606829","date":"2024-04-26","text":"Texture test!","topic":"texture","status":"ref","where":"planet.html","note":"星球贴图测试：绿色陆地、浅色岸、海；重构版的星球没有贴图","project":"next"},{"id":"1781405550061687016","date":"2024-04-19","text":"Ok this might not look like much but I've got seamless patch blending! Some of the patches are projected (like the grass and the water) and some are manually UV-mapped (like the shoreline). With some good textures and some height based blending this is gonna be great.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"顶面画成扇形：中心本格颜色，角上取\"共用此角、同高度、非河道\"的所有顶面颜色平均 → 草 / 苔 / 沙之间无缝过渡","project":"next"},{"id":"1769691526924292506","date":"2024-03-18","text":"Mega river system! I've had trouble making good rivers before. Now I've sort of special cased the rivers by collapsing them depth-first to let them wiggle real far, and then the rest is collapsed breadth-first, making nice gentle slopes that only occasionally meet steep cliffs.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/generate.js","note":"河流深度优先坍缩、其余广度优先成缓坡","project":"next"},{"id":"1769641473895432220","date":"2024-03-18","text":"In cute tile based planets like this you often get a \"mushrooming\" issue where tall mountains get weirdly wide. I managed to mitigate this by a relax pass where all module-containing cells try to achieve their desired shape and size. Note the cells on the top left contracting.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/sphere/planet.js（cornerPositions）","note":"防蘑菇化：有东西的格子的边按海平面长度当弹簧松弛；高台面积膨胀 1.90× → 1.35×","project":"next"},{"id":"1768627849529893109","date":"2024-03-15","text":"For reasons I will not be explaining at this point I've gone and put this on a sphere","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/sphere/planet.js · planet.html","note":"放到球面：对偶多边形格子 + 偶数层台阶的小星球","project":"next"},{"id":"1765115069837221962","date":"2024-03-05","text":"Here, I'm visualizing the recursive tree parsing as it adds new rects. Note that when the board is more fragmented the arm tends to have more fingers.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"grids.html（图集打包）","note":"递归解析树：细线 = 树的切分；板子越碎叶子越多（页面显示叶子数）","project":"next"},{"id":"1765041830461055127","date":"2024-03-05","text":"Now supports removing rects too! The bin space gets quite fragmented after a while though.. I've tried to optimize it on the fly but I can't figure out how to when it get sort of interlocked. Still packs tight though!","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"src/core/atlas.js（free）· grids.html","note":"能删除矩形；兄弟都空就合并回父节点，碎片不一直累积","project":"next"},{"id":"1764958522398146667","date":"2024-03-05","text":"A cute binary tree rect packer. Generating the placement attempts is kinda brute force (to get into all the nooks and crannies), but then it's using the tree properly for fast collision checks. I think this is the first time I've actually written a proper space partion tree. Fun.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/core/atlas.js · grids.html（图集打包）","note":"二叉树矩形打包：生成放置尝试是暴力的，碰撞检测用树加速；网格实验室里实时演示","project":"next"},{"id":"1758251637280268481","date":"2024-02-15","text":"It's simply a stack of planes sampling an SDF I had laying around. Gives a much more fluid vibe than the basic flipped mesh approach in Bad North and Townscaper","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/watervol.js（开关「体积浅水」）","note":"海岸 2D 距离场（两遍 chamfer）+ 6 张平面叠在海面上，每张只画距离 < 阈值的一圈，阈值随噪声与时间起伏 → 一圈圈会流动的浅滩等深线","project":"next"},{"id":"1758250248483278925","date":"2024-02-15","text":"New water reflection I'm quite happy with","topic":"water","status":"ref","where":"src/world/view.js（reflection）","note":"新的水面倒影；重构版仍是翻转网格的倒影","project":"next"},{"id":"1751945034851570056","date":"2024-01-29","text":"Some nice new highlights when the island is backlit. Achieved by simply adding another inverted mesh outline layer that shows up when looking into the sun. And masked by shadows, of course.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/outline.js","note":"两层反向外壳：墨线（固定像素宽）+ 更宽的逆光亮边，只在镜头朝太阳、迎光一侧出现；阴影遮罩用朝下程度近似","project":"next"},{"id":"1751932427272909032","date":"2024-01-29","text":"I can now force specific modules to appear. To do this I first generate the specific bit of grid they need. A large module like this would be highly unlikely to appear by chance on a random grid.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js（forceChurch）","note":"强制模块：先压平台地，再放教堂（中殿 + 钟楼）","project":"next"},{"id":"1727324352264474664","date":"2023-11-22","text":"Yeah that actually looks pretty good. I did not expect that.","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1727315611959865407","date":"2023-11-22","text":"I've shipped two whole games with orbital cameras and not once have I previously though about adding motion blur smear. What a fool I am.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（#smear）","note":"轨道相机的运动模糊拖影：转得快时把上一帧按转速半透明叠上来（面板「运动模糊」）","project":"next"},{"id":"1724449858369568780","date":"2023-11-14","text":"Ok, here's a small example. The button toggles a ScriptableObject bool. The FloatSelectNode component listens to that ScriptableObject, and then a series of node-like components end up moving a piece of UI","topic":"tools","status":"ref","where":"","note":"Unity ScriptableObject + 节点式组件做 UI 逻辑；引擎专用，记作参考","project":"next"},{"id":"1714613599035863191","date":"2023-10-18","text":"Another strange texturing style. This time trying to look a bit like abstract fields. A nice thing is they show the game tiles quite clearly. In the end I probably want a mix where some areas are more man made and others more natural.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"textures.html（抽象田地）","note":"像抽象田地的贴图：每块地一个条纹方向，能清楚看出格子","project":"next"},{"id":"1712088611934371876","date":"2023-10-11","text":"Another take on a palette authoring tool","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（调色板）","note":"调色板编辑器：四角取色的渐变方块 + 往白色收的三角（工具页，没有接回游戏调色板）","project":"next"},{"id":"1710031224838771027","date":"2023-10-05","text":"Ok here's a probably horrible way to author color volumes. The idea is to properly define the whole color possibility space for each feature","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（调色板）","note":"颜色体积编辑：给地物定义完整的可用颜色空间（四角插值），采样出 15 色","project":"next"},{"id":"1708815475801505819","date":"2023-10-02","text":"a cool cliff I came across","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js","note":"海中石柱：浪蚀台脚 + 蘑菇帽","project":"next"},{"id":"1707497006640365880","date":"2023-09-28","text":"And here's a couple more being generated","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1707490932017279035","date":"2023-09-28","text":"They are of course 100% texture, painted onto a fairly low, poly mesh. I keep thinking I'm gonna need to give em some volume with billboard sprites, but now I'm not so sure anymore. Especially with the lil' shadows, they look quite volumetric as they are.","topic":"light","status":"ref","where":"","note":"100% 画在低模上的贴图（画面：橙黄色的台地，三角线框清晰）；重构版是顶点色","project":"next"},{"id":"1707490274425884929","date":"2023-09-28","text":"I added back the lil' shrubbery at the edges of things for like the 3rd time","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"崖顶线（顶面边上邻居更低）每隔一段一丛灌木，往里收一点；颜色大多绿，少数橄榄 / 赭色","project":"next"},{"id":"1705195380457996629","date":"2023-09-22","text":"I tamed the texture based surface shadows a bit, so the shadow casting height is independent of the z test height. Now I only get shadows over grass-cliff edges and under roofs. It has some artifacts across UV borders, but it's quite subtle so I might not actually have to fix it.","topic":"light","status":"partial","where":"src/world/view.js（体素阴影）","note":"投影高度和深度测试高度分开、只在草-崖边和屋檐下出阴影：思路学了，实现是逐顶点版","project":"next"},{"id":"1704246032626762189","date":"2023-09-19","text":"Ok, I think maybe this is a bit of a sweet spot. It's got a nice variable density texture to it. There are some height segmentation lines to help with readability, but they don't feel too synthetic.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（疏密 + 等高线）","note":"疏密变化的细笔触 + 高度分段线（等高线，用 fwidth 保持 1 像素）","project":"next"},{"id":"1704218784028905984","date":"2023-09-19","text":"I tried some texture based shadows. Note the shadows on the grass and along the roof edges. Looks kinda cool, but feels a bit too 3D for what I'm going for this time. I feel like it clashes with lines, and I like lines more.","topic":"light","status":"partial","where":"src/world/view.js（体素阴影）","note":"贴图阴影（草上、屋檐下）：重构版用逐顶点体素阴影代替，不是贴图","project":"next"},{"id":"1703750394164199473","date":"2023-09-18","text":"Looking at my procedural stylized ground texturing again. Really like the swirly blobbyness of these. They feel kind of damp for some reason.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（BLOTCH_GLSL）· textures.html","note":"旋涡状团块的地面笔触：域扭曲噪声量化成三档（主场景面板「地面笔触」）","project":"next"},{"id":"1699146321318314094","date":"2023-09-05","text":"Oh! And now I finally figured out how to make non-straight sedimentary lines! Most of the texturing math is kinda linear, so I though the lines had to be linear too. But I could (obviously) just make the whole world wobbly, do the texturing math, then simply undo the wobble.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"把世界弄弯、算贴图、再弯回去：沉积线高度 = 层中线 + 世界空间噪声(x,z)，相邻崖面同一噪声 → 连续起伏的岩层","project":"next"},{"id":"1699038611125985317","date":"2023-09-05","text":"Looking att sedimentation lines again. Helps make large cliffs more interesting. Also makes their shape a bit more readable maybe.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"沉积线让大崖壁更耐看、形体更好读：每层一条，贴在崖面外侧","project":"next"},{"id":"1696896119794479541","date":"2023-08-30","text":"On the other hand, I've always wanted to make a game in the Art Nouveau style. This might be a good fit. Look how neat and controlled the grass blotches bleed over the cliff edges.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"草顶面、邻居更低的边：沿崖面往下垂一段圆润的草色舌头，深度 = 噪声 × sin(πu)^0.6，不是每段都有","project":"next"},{"id":"1696864977171189980","date":"2023-08-30","text":"I'm slowly emerging from a huge refactoring... While this here is not exactly the look I'm going for, it's showing off a big improvement to the texturing. I'm now able to draw with much bigger blotches without the blotches bleeding across and messing up important edges.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（blotchTone 按高度层换噪声）","note":"大色块不渗过重要的边：每一层台阶一套噪声偏移，色块在崖边断开","project":"next"},{"id":"1677242779162877952","date":"2023-07-07","text":"I am (once again) rewriting my generic triangle graph system to (hopefully) be more robust and generic. Here's a stress test where I'm adding random verts, making sure the graph stays mainifold and delauney-ish along the way.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/trigraph.js","note":"通用三角图：增量 Delaunay + 流形 / 近 Delaunay 体检","project":"next"},{"id":"1671840905957978113","date":"2023-06-22","text":"Hmm.. I thought it was gonna be too wacky but maybe it's kinda cool","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1671808851895627776","date":"2023-06-22","text":"If your terrain generator supports overhangs you gotta flaunt it. I don't make the rules, but I do follow them.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js · terrainmesh.js","note":"悬垂：崖顶外伸、底下空、下面的地照样画","project":"next"},{"id":"1670794261669769217","date":"2023-06-19","text":"Oh, and I finally got this lovely rock feature to show up! When working with WFC, sometimes you build a cool tile and it wont show up in forever, since it's conditions are so specific. You forget about it, and then suddenly: poof!","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js","note":"天然石拱","project":"next"},{"id":"1670790425232175108","date":"2023-06-19","text":"I'm prepping for a talk in Cambridge next week, thus all the gifs. I made my generator also output pure triangle/hex and square grids, to illustrate why I'm going for my mixed approach.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"grids.html","note":"纯三角 / 纯方格 / 混合三种网格对比","project":"next"},{"id":"1670725072540106755","date":"2023-06-19","text":"Here's a comparison showing no-, dumb- and hierarchical smoothing. The hierarchical smoothing helps preserve the intent of the input-tiles while smoothing out the jankyness from the weird underlying grid and from the limited slope angles in the input tileset","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"对比三种：不平滑 / dumb（海岸被啃、崖顶塌）/ 层级（海岸圆滑、崖顶与房子保持锐利）。「地形」场景勾掉「层级平滑」即可对比","project":"next"},{"id":"1670720537662836736","date":"2023-06-19","text":"I smooth my mesh according to an edge type hierarchy. Black is hard, red is game-tile-border and blue is material-border. Verts only get to pull at equal or lower order verts, and only along the appropriate edges","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"切面上分级：钉住(外圈/房子 tile/分叉点) > 崖顶线 > 崖脚线 > 内部；轮廓点只沿同级边、只被同级或更高级拉（Taubin 不缩），内部点吸收位移。画面里黑=硬、红=tile 边、蓝=材质边","project":"next"},{"id":"1670064751181791233","date":"2023-06-17","text":"I figured out how to mimic Thread.Sleep() in Burst! Just store time in a static unsafe NativeArray! Then you can write to it from the main thread and read from it inside a job! Probably super bad in many ways but good enough for visualization and debug!","topic":"tools","status":"ref","where":"","note":"Burst 里模拟 Thread.Sleep 来慢放生成过程；我们首页的「完整管线示例 · 一步加一层」是同一目的","project":"next"},{"id":"1669315384619540487","date":"2023-06-15","text":"The generator consistently spits out pretty cool islands now","topic":"terrain","status":"ref","where":"src/terrain/generate.js","note":"生成器稳定出好看的岛（展示）","project":"next"},{"id":"1666429884208381953","date":"2023-06-07","text":"I've been banging my head against various shore line rendering options for a good week now. Gonna stick with this for now I think, which is basically just a refined version of what I did for Bad North and Townscaper.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"岸线渲染：Bad North / Townscaper 那套的改良版（距离场浪裙）","project":"next"},{"id":"1664566546683899905","date":"2023-06-02","text":"Here's a distance field-like mesh skirt solution very similar to Townscaper and Bad North. It works for calm waters I guess... But I would like something with a bit more punch this time. A bit more crashing waves.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"类距离场的浪裙：栅格化陆地 + chamfer 距离，外推点按真实距离放置，海湾不会折叠","project":"next"},{"id":"1664565063552847873","date":"2023-06-02","text":"I'm trying out using a shader based fluid simulation. But I'm skeptical. It seems to need 32 bit float render targets, and I don't trust that those will work across platforms. Might also be a challenge to tweak, stylize, and feed back to CPU if needed.","topic":"water","status":"ref","where":"","note":"着色器流体模拟试验；作者自己也怀疑（要 32 位浮点渲染目标、难调、难回读），没采用","project":"next"},{"id":"1654401054828638214","date":"2023-05-05","text":"An quaint island being procedurally generated","topic":"terrain","status":"ref","where":"src/terrain/generate.js","note":"一座岛的生成过程：三角底网 → 线框崖 → 上色","project":"next"},{"id":"1593215065423245313","date":"2022-11-17","text":"Making a lil dynamic sprite packer, able to add and remove sprite allotments at runtime. I had one of these in Bad North and found it very useful. Here, the sprites are baked live from meshes. So I guess it's basically impostors. Though I expect to use it for much else too.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/core/atlas.js","note":"二叉树矩形打包：按剩余较多的方向切；free() 后兄弟都空就向上合并；impostor 烘焙从这里分配格子","project":"next"},{"id":"1590674061092212738","date":"2022-11-10","text":"In the vertex shader, my grass gets to sample that contrast texture both where they stand, and also raycast into the background. The outline strength is determined by the difference between these two samples! Not perfect, but pretty good! Not too jittery when turning the camera","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"草的描边强度 = 站立处与背景的反差：外轮廓在崖边加粗","project":"next"},{"id":"1590669875869286400","date":"2022-11-10","text":"An early look at grass billboards. I really like how they add a completely new kind of shape and detail frequency.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"草丛广告牌：扇贝边叶丛（5 个圆的并集 + 叶瓣弧线墨线），一簇簇堆在崖脚 / 崖顶 / 坡上；之前做成尖草叶是错的，已重做","project":"next"},{"id":"1584623053061099520","date":"2022-10-24","text":"I wrote a thing to splice houses into the terrain. Mostly, the houses are part of pre-build tiles, but would be useful insert them at will too. You can kinda see the structure of my mesh system and mesh algoritms by how the yellow lines are rotating around the verts.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/world/scenes.js","note":"4 房子拼进地形（台地排屋、海湾码头、跨峡谷的拱）","project":"next"},{"id":"1582757294672314368","date":"2022-10-19","text":"I'm seeing if my light volume approach can work with point lights too. The low resolution is noticeable for sure. Especially when you move em around like this. But if you keep em big and soft and somewhat still I think it's gonna be good.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/lightvolume.js（point）+ 开关「点光源」","note":"点光源进同一个体积：距离衰减 + 遮挡步进；\"keep em big and soft\" → 半径大、二次衰减","project":"next"},{"id":"1582293326815862786","date":"2022-10-18","text":"I thought it would be too expensive to properly evaluate each tile placement. But! While the number of possible tiles is indeed very large, it is actually quite small around the collapsed edge! Thus, my algorithm now tries to expand (and interconnect) a simplified nav graph.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/world/navgraph.js","note":"简化导航图：同高连片 = 区域节点，Dijkstra 最短路树","project":"next"},{"id":"1580846877855338497","date":"2022-10-14","text":"Here's the slowed down bounce sequence. You can see how the mega texture and the light volume affect each other back and forth. After about the 3rd bounce, further bounces are not noticeable.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/lightvolume.js（bounceChange）","note":"逐次反弹的变化量记在 bounceChange：实测 [0.49, 0.07, 0.02] —— 和原片一样，第 3 次之后看不出来","project":"next"},{"id":"1580845127207387137","date":"2022-10-14","text":"1st texture here is an sdf volume. The distance lives in the alpha, but RG actually reference UVs in the mega texture! 2nd is a baked 6 directional light volume, raycast against the sdf, sampling the mega texture using the UVs where it hits the sdf. 3rd is the lit mega texture","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/lightvolume.js","note":"6 向光体积；原片用 SDF 体积 + 指回 mega texture 的 UV，我们直接用体素格的反照率（每格一色），效果同理","project":"next"},{"id":"1580835075629133825","date":"2022-10-14","text":"I always write my own lighting solutions. I've had some really naive ad hoc color bleeding in my (very fake) GI before, but this is my first decent attempt to actually have the light *bounce*","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/lightvolume.js + view.js（bakeGI，开关「间接光」）","note":"光体积 + 多次反弹：体素化 → 直射（朝太阳步进）→ 6 向收集反弹 3 次 → 顶点三线性取样，混进 indirectDiffuse；阴影里泛出地面/墙的颜色","project":"next"},{"id":"1580162341668237312","date":"2022-10-12","text":"I start with a very basic Marching Cubes mesh from a bunch of spheres. I mark the edges between triangles that are closest to different spheres. Then I run an iterative relax algorithm where those hard edges are like rubber bands, and the rest is sort of a like a balloon.","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"团块的轮廓用反向外壳墨线（跟随「墨线」开关）；原片是在三角形之间标边","project":"next"},{"id":"1580158269267406849","date":"2022-10-12","text":"Can you make good looking foliage from Marching Cubes-blobs? Maybe?","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"树冠 = 几个球融在一起，法线取离整团中心的方向与自身法线的混合 → 像 Marching Cubes 团块一样整团受光；三种树冠变体","project":"next"},{"id":"1579483114178768898","date":"2022-10-10","text":"Obviously, it's all tile-based. I went through a major rewrite to combine an irregular grid (like in Townscaper) with multi-cell tiles (like in Bad North). Note how one of the house tiles even cover both a square tile AND a triangular tile","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js · core/grid.js","note":"多格 tile：同一栋房子相邻格之间不起墙，三角格 + 方格拼一栋","project":"next"},{"id":"1579478470098243584","date":"2022-10-10","text":"To make the cliffs look more organic, I'm doing some pretty radical cage deformation on the cells.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"笼形变形：崖顶线沿外法线随高度内收（下宽上窄），加随高度缓变的噪声让崖壁扭动；位移有上限防翻折","project":"next"},{"id":"1579474420749725696","date":"2022-10-10","text":"I'm back on the island generation","topic":"terrain","status":"ref","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"岛屿生成回归：线框 → 上色的台地岛","project":"next"},{"id":"1490068909042642944","date":"2022-02-05","text":"Late night cryptic graph tweet","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"","note":"深夜的神秘图：一圈圈同心的环形图","project":"next"},{"id":"1489193847422865410","date":"2022-02-03","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1482346496460828674","date":"2022-01-15","text":"I created a dedicated contrast texture system for the lines: an iterative simulation on the triangles that starts random and then tries to make contrasted edges different, and non-contrasted edges similar. A byproduct is a beautiful color gradient that help express connectivity","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（反差线）","note":"专门的反差贴图：三角形上迭代，有反差的边推开（权重 1）、没反差的拉近（权重 4）；实测 80 条该画的边全画出、误画约 5 条；副产品是表达连通性的渐变色","project":"next"},{"id":"1482011744843223042","date":"2022-01-14","text":"Ok, I stumbled on a pretty cool art style now. Here, I'm creating pixel thin lines from contrasts in my procedural normal map. I should probably move to a bespoke contrast texture (to get more deliberate control over the lines). But I gotta say this looks pretty promising.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（反差线）· src/world/outline.js","note":"从\"反差\"生成一像素细线：场景里的墨线按法线 / 高度反差画；实验室里按三角形反差模拟画","project":"next"},{"id":"1481661852887265288","date":"2022-01-13","text":"Yet another light baker. Actually does some ray marching, but still pretty ad hoc. The textures are: 1. Normals (procedurally painted in big chunky strokes) 2. 3D Signed Distance Field 3. 3D Ambient Occlusion in positive and negative X,Y and Z","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/light/lightvolume.js（ao）","note":"又一个烘焙器：法线 / SDF / 正负 XYZ 六向 AO。六向 AO 已算（ao 字段，开口方向数/6），3D SDF 没单独存","project":"next"},{"id":"1480635131614355459","date":"2022-01-10","text":"More experiments in procedural texturing of procedural islands. Still very early, but I do like these big paint blotches. They hide the polys well and they would be hard to achieve with other means. Definitely need a proper lighting system though. And probably some outlines.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（地面笔触）","note":"大块颜料斑藏住多边形：量化的三档明暗只画在朝上的草色面","project":"next"},{"id":"1478114309263839244","date":"2022-01-03","text":"Yeah that's good enough for now. I quite like how the radial (instead of directional) size-sorting looks. Gonna make for some visually pleasing textures with that big coherent chunk in the middle.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（径向排序）","note":"笔触从大到小、从中心螺旋找空位：中间一大块整齐的，越往外越碎","project":"next"},{"id":"1471817524148940807","date":"2021-12-17","text":"Some rocky islands. Trying to make the grid natural and readable, yet funky. Square, yet hex.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/grid.js（buildMixedGrid）","note":"\"方，又带六边形味\"的岩岛：三角 + 方格混合网格","project":"next"},{"id":"1466059785703460870","date":"2021-12-01","text":"Oh. What's this? A free Townscaper web demo, playable straight in the browser: http:// oskarstalberg.com/Townscaper/ 🕊️💦🌊🏡🏤⛪️🏤🏡🌊💦🕊️","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1459169210752507904","date":"2021-11-12","text":"And another","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1458921394855718917","date":"2021-11-11","text":"I'm exploring the Half Edge data structure. Feels like a really lightweight, powerful and versatile way of representing topology. A big thanks to everyone suggesting I look into it.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/grid.js · finishGrid()","note":"半边结构（格子是任意多边形，edgeTwins）","project":"next"},{"id":"1448039167057879048","date":"2021-10-12","text":"Imma talk about my new island generator at Sweden Game Conference (@SwedenGameArena) on Friday (no idea if its gonna be recorded). Naturally, I'm preparing by implementing some nice timing and visualization.","topic":"terrain","status":"ref","where":"src/ui/walkthrough.js","note":"岛屿生成的计时 + 可视化（线框逐步出现）；重构版的「完整管线示例」一步一层，同一用意","project":"next"},{"id":"1447496205282549761","date":"2021-10-11","text":"The base graph is just a humble irregular triangle grid","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/grid.js（buildMixedGrid）","note":"底图就是一张不规则三角网","project":"next"},{"id":"1447494168448753667","date":"2021-10-11","text":"Long time fans of the show will not be surprised to learn that this is indeed running on tile based WFC. This time around, I'm getting the best of both worlds by using a mix of triangular and square tiles. (The squares are cut along each diagonal to create 4 triangles though)","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/core/grid.js · buildMixedGrid()（左上角切换网格）","note":"三角 + 方格混合网格（新项目）","project":"next"},{"id":"1447488323845509121","date":"2021-10-11","text":"I'm able to do a couple of things here I've always wanted to, but never been able to before: - Properly combine seamless soft slopes with distinct sharp cliffs. - Erosion valid terrain with no local minimums. - Get the best of both square tiles and triangular tiles","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/generate.js","note":"2 台地 / 悬崖（偶数层量化）+ 沙滩","project":"next"},{"id":"1447483550257799171","date":"2021-10-11","text":"I regret to inform you that I've relapsed into procedural island generation","topic":"terrain","status":"ref","where":"src/terrain/generate.js","note":"又回到岛屿生成（画面：暗色岩块 + 蓝色河网的岛，再到线框图）","project":"next"},{"id":"1430227487376781317","date":"2021-08-24","text":"Plus you can change the in-game textures now! So I guess the game is now (in the most liberal use of the word) \"moddable\"","topic":"texture","status":"ref","where":"","note":"可以换游戏内贴图了（画面：在 Photoshop 里改 Townscaper 的总贴图）。重构版没有总贴图，不适用","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1430224300003545091","date":"2021-08-24","text":"If you've been waiting for the Townscaper mesh exporter, you can now try it out in the public beta branch on Steam. There's a bunch of other subtle changes and optimizations too, but nothing major. Please do let me know if you run into any issues!","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"src/tools/objexport.js + 首页右上 ⇩ 按钮","note":"导出 .OBJ：合并网格写成 v（带顶点色）/ vn / f，相同顶点量化合并（35745 → 25296 顶点）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1427721874490933250","date":"2021-08-17","text":"Here's a very quick technical test. Though this one is continuously adding decals, so it looks a bit like claymation or line boil. Might be softer than what I'd be going for, but it was an easy style to throw together. And obviously you'd need some padding for the seams.","topic":"texture","status":"ref","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（血迹贴花）","note":"不断叠加贴花的技术测试，像黏土动画 / 抖动线；北境的血迹是累积贴花，但没有这种画风","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1410697531424714752","date":"2021-07-01","text":"Townscaper is now on GoG! https:// gog.com/game/townscaper","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1401145625572425728","date":"2021-06-05","text":"Meshes in Townscaper are kept small to rely on Unity's dynamic mesh batching. This approach was not performant enough on the Switch though, so I wrote a mesh merger to do my own batching instead. It made a huge difference, something like tripling the rendering speed.","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"src/core/meshwriter.js（整座小镇一个合并网格）","note":"网格合并：我们从一开始就是一个 MeshWriter 写出的一个大网格、一次 draw call，等于原片在 Switch 上补的 mesh merger","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1384958097542819845","date":"2021-04-21","text":"I wrote a script to trace topologically straight lines across the Townscaper grid. I think I'll use it for a thing in the gamepad controls and possibly some drag-to-paint mode.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/grid.js（traceStraight）· grids.html","note":"拓扑直线：每到四边形从对边出去（手柄 / 拖动连刷）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1371460793032716290","date":"2021-03-15","text":"I got it working within the duration of exactly 1 kid nap","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1371191380773629956","date":"2021-03-14","text":"Yeah this is gonna be pretty good","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1370772056279805953","date":"2021-03-13","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1344290848180203523","date":"2020-12-30","text":"A rare look at Townscapers sophisticated QA process","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1338829205157646336","date":"2020-12-15","text":"Apparently, one way to do Delaunay Triangulation on a sphere is to do it on a Stereographic Projection. (Many people have done this before me, so it's nothing new). My points are sorted vertically, which means radially, which makes the algorithm faster. Here's what it looks like:","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/trigraph.js · src/sphere/planet.js","note":"球面 Delaunay = 在球极投影平面上做；点按半径排序再增量插入（planet.html 右下角）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1338825080844021760","date":"2020-12-15","text":"Apropos of nothing, a take on the ancient issue of generating nice triangulated spheres 1. Random points 2. Space out the points 3. Triangulate 4. Relax using the triangles Unclear if I'll use this for anything helpful sources: https:// redblobgames.com/x/1842-delauna y-voronoi-sphere/ … https:// newcastle.edu.au/__data/assets/ pdf_file/0017/22508/13_A-fast-algorithm-for-constructing-Delaunay-triangulations-in-the-plane.pdf …","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/sphere/planet.js · planet.html","note":"球面三角网：随机点 → 散开 → 三角化 → 按三角形松弛（页面可逐步看）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1332410042784641026","date":"2020-11-27","text":"How the infinite grid is relaxed and kept seamless: The grid is made of Patches. Adjacent triplets form Clusters. Clusters and Patches are relaxed independently. Each Vert is a triangular interpolation its representation in the closest 2 Clusters and the Patch wherein it sits.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/infinite.js · grids.html","note":"块（Patch）+ 簇（Cluster）各自松弛，顶点 = 所在块 + 最近两簇的重心插值；实测两侧位置差 4e-15、无翻折","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1331905048801144836","date":"2020-11-26","text":"Townscaper now has lighthouses! This pattern required more code rewrite than seems reasonable. Luckily, I got some slight optimization out of it too. https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/lighthouse.js（开关「灯塔」）","note":"海边、≥5 层、每个邻格都矮 2 层以上的一格粗塔 → 自动加灯室（窗棂 + 暖光）、平台栏杆、红尖顶，夜里一道光束绕塔转","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1313841094069817344","date":"2020-10-07","text":"Because I'm quite proud of my lighting (and because Townscaper is basically just a tech demo anyway) I added texture-only and light-only render modes","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js","note":"只看贴图 / 只看光照两种渲染模式","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1313840428685447170","date":"2020-10-07","text":"I added some sunlight (with shadows) and a gizmo to control it","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/ui/learnpanel.js（太阳方位）· view.setSunAngle()","note":"阳光 + 阴影 + 控制小工具：面板里拖「太阳方位」，影子、墨线、逆光一起转；白天 / 黄昏 / 夜晚（夜里窗户亮）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1313837640366596096","date":"2020-10-07","text":"I just pushed an update to Townscaper. You can now build flying towns (if you find any of the perfect loops I've scattered across the grid) https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/core/grid.js（traceStraight）","note":"完美环：直线绕回起点时检测出来；飞岛玩法没做","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1310503825510367232","date":"2020-09-28","text":"Ok, I tried the mixed perspective. Note how houses further away are smaller, yet the vertical lines stay straight and parallel. It's definitely not a good fit for Townscaper, but might work well if I make another Bad North-ish game with a hearty mix of 3D meshes and billboards.","topic":"build","status":"ref","where":"","note":"混合透视：远处房子变小但竖线保持平行。需要自定义投影矩阵，记作相机参考","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1305951750638231552","date":"2020-09-15","text":"To soften it up a bit, I'm trying out a penumbra approach where I draw the shadow thrice, once normal, once pulled in slightly and once with big voxels. I think I like it. (here, the shadow is shown darker than it should be to demonstrate the effect)","topic":"light","status":"partial","where":"src/world/view.js（shadows）","note":"半影：阴影画三遍（正常、稍收、大体素）。重构版用 PCF 软阴影，没有三遍叠","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1305948413872267265","date":"2020-09-15","text":"I'm exploring cast shadows. They have to be quite subtle and soft to fit the style. It does seems like they should be fast enough for mobile too if I only update them on command after a regeneration.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js","note":"柔和投影：实时 PCF 软阴影，海面有投影接收层","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1302686201401442309","date":"2020-09-06","text":"A smoothing and inversion bug I came across while playing with the grid generation. The inverted patches collapse into a mess, but are stretched out when interpolating to fit with their neighbors. And the poor non-inverted patches need to stretch real far to pick up the slack","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"src/core/infinite.js（verify）","note":"平滑 + 翻折 bug 的画面：翻折的块塌成一团、邻块被拉长。我们每组外圈钉住，verify() 统计翻折数（实测 0）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1301816247479345152","date":"2020-09-04","text":"Some are asking for the option to use regular grids. Now, that's (obviously) against the Townscaper design philosophy. However, I am thinking of sprinkling the current generated grid with random patches of hand crafted grid, like little gems to find and build your tempels upon","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"","note":"在生成网格里撒手工的规则网格块（八边形放射状广场）当彩蛋；未实现","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1298689301488775169","date":"2020-08-26","text":"Flat texture, shaded, lighting only, and my AO baking mesh. I'm thinking of adding some little widgets like this to give people a peek at how things work. Perhaps hide them behind a break-glass-to-push-button widget.","topic":"light","status":"partial","where":"src/world/view.js（lightonly / ao）","note":"平涂 / 着色 / 只看光照 / AO 烘焙网格四种视图：前三种有（面板开关），AO 烘焙网格的可视化没做","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1290997501332525056","date":"2020-08-05","text":"#Townscaper is now properly released on Mac on Steam! To celebrate the occasion, I added some garden paths. Go get it: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"后院 ≥6 格时按格心协方差求主轴，离主轴（和副轴）< 0.2 的格子铺浅色石板小径；小径上不种树","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1279107097108635649","date":"2020-07-03","text":"Here's a tour of the puzzle pieces that make up #Townscaper. To date, there are 545 of them.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js（sigColor）","note":"模块签名调试色：同一种邻居占用涂同一种颜色","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1277554535297236994","date":"2020-06-29","text":"Ok I'm gonna try something that probably wont work: if you wanna help me translate Townscaper to your language, I simply made the localization spreadsheet public: https:// docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d /1sKbLTWhlpa3CcpOKBnACkJ1kl7_Bi2HvW78gaEQUo1c/edit?usp=sharing …","topic":"tools","status":"ref","where":"","note":"把本地化表格公开让玩家帮忙翻译；左右箭头切语言。我们的界面只有中文，记作参考","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1275089608758484992","date":"2020-06-22","text":"It has not escaped some of you that I have yet to release Townscaper. I have an important (secret) business thing to consider, and instead of making a decision I've been making church doors and and ladders. (but do wishlist though: https:// steamcommunity.com/app/1291340 )","topic":"build","status":"na","where":"","note":"发布前的商务说明，无技术内容","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1273520600221433857","date":"2020-06-18","text":"Butterflies fly quite different from birds. Mine loosely orbit a potential landing spot, and drift by randomly switching that spot. Additional world space noise adds variability but also coherence (without boiding) (as always, please wishlist: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ … )","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"落点 = 小花 + 后院；每只绕落点松散转圈（半径 0.12–0.27），3–9 秒随机换附近落点；速度叠世界空间噪声 → 同一片的蝴蝶往同一边飘；翅膀扇动","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1270725616430530566","date":"2020-06-10","text":"You all keep pestering me to release this when I hadn't even added butterflies yet. But do indeed go wishlist: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"蝴蝶在后院花园上空飞（画面：环形排屋围着的花园）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1260586697538113537","date":"2020-05-13","text":"Making a trailer is a ton of work. But the good news is I can use the undo/redo stack for snappier and more directed building footage.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/world/app.js（replay）· 工具栏 ⟲","note":"用撤销栈录预告片：⟲ 按钮从场景载入后第一步开始逐步回放，每步照常弹出、水花、音效","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1259838941299183619","date":"2020-05-11","text":"In code, these are called \"Italian Wires\"","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"从外墙中点沿外法线走 0.6–2.2，碰到另一栋 ≥3 层的房子就拉一根悬链线，每隔 ~0.085 挂一面三角彩旗；整根绳中间摆得最大","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1258421104756097029","date":"2020-05-07","text":"We were long overdue for some splashier splashes","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js","note":"第一块落进水（之前顶层 0）或拆到水面：一圈白色泡沫环向外扩、变淡 + 26 颗飞沫（重力下落、落水即灭）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1258005604066627586","date":"2020-05-06","text":"Here's that but in Townscaper. And Triangular.","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"","note":"同一套东西搬进 Townscaper、换三角网格（灯塔塔楼）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1257213678056857600","date":"2020-05-04","text":"Alrighty. First 20 people to reply gets a b e t a k e y *steam on windows for now","topic":"build","status":"na","where":"","note":"发 beta key，无技术内容","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1246074663546916873","date":"2020-04-03","text":"The props now animate when they appear and disappear. This was much trickier than I anticipated.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js","note":"合并网格里没法单独动道具 → 把\"最近 8 次长高的格子\"作为 uniform 交给主材质顶点着色器：格心附近、原高度以上的顶点按弹性曲线从 0.35 长到 1（略过冲）；拆除补一团上飘的灰尘","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1244892370392489989","date":"2020-03-31","text":"Better Birdies: 🐦 More bird shaped 🐦 Only has outlines when sitting 🐦 Shuffle about more 🐦 Has reflections 🐦 Flowier flight","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/life/birds.js","note":"海鸥：屋脊顶点找栖位成排停（有描边、会挪步）；起飞 → 绕镇流动地飞（扇翅 / 滑翔）→ 落回空栖位；水里有倒影","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1243228419162341379","date":"2020-03-26","text":"Some moody clouds","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"地平线外一圈放大很多的灰色云 impostor（和树、云共用同一套烘焙）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1242824460325052417","date":"2020-03-25","text":"Finally making some proper UI. Turns out you can make a boring list of buttons playful by just tilting them slightly.","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"ui.html（斜按钮）","note":"按钮随机转 ±2.4° 并错开几像素，悬停摆正放大","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1241096929490149376","date":"2020-03-20","text":"It has been brought to my attention that not all of you are familiar with my every-other-pixel-is-a-line tech. I make the UVs speed past every 2nd pixel before sampling. It's core to my art style and what lets me get away with one 128² texture and crisp antialiasing up close.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（隔像素一条线）","note":"128² 贴图里每隔一个像素是线像素；采样前重映射 UV，让线像素在屏幕上永远只占 1 像素——放大不变粗、不糊","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1241046107125399552","date":"2020-03-20","text":"I moved my plants to a 32² corner on the 128² texture I'm using for everything else. Plus they now also use the every-other-pixel-is-a-line tech, so everything is crisp and nice up close","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"植物贴图并进 128² 总图集的 32² 角，并用隔像素一条线的描边技术，近看也清楚；画面：后院沿墙一排圆灌木、矮墙、盆栽树","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1239901715266244609","date":"2020-03-17","text":"If you're hunkered down hiding from the virus (as you should be) and need something to do, I'll be shameless enough to plug our last project, the minimalist strategy game Bad North. Available on PC, Mac, IOs, Android, Switch, PS4, Xbox. @BadNorthGame https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North_Jotunn_Edition/ …","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1238474550511308800","date":"2020-03-13","text":"I needed some more greenery, so now if you build an enclosed area it becomes a backyard!","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"被房子围住、到不了水边的地面层自动变成后院：草坪 + 树","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1237305125070426112","date":"2020-03-10","text":"Obviously, a big benefit of this is that with white finally in my palette, I can properly show off the colored \"bounce\" \"light\" of my custom realtime \"lighting\" system.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/bake.js","note":"白墙旁边的红墙会把一点红色反到白墙上","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1237293295887319040","date":"2020-03-10","text":"More colors! I had been assuming the combinatorics would go crazy and that all my assumptions would break if I introduced more colors, but I was wrong and it was fine.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/core/palette.js","note":"更多颜色：15 个色槽（画面左边一列 15 色）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1215644531221311488","date":"2020-01-10","text":"The technical solution is almost the same as in Bad North. One big difference is that the bright colors wouldn't let me get a way with a monochrome reflection, so I had to figure out this somewhat abstract flat colored mid point. (Also, the wave skirt stretches further this time)","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js","note":"倒影不用单色，而是\"物体色与水色之间的扁平中间色\"；浪裙更宽（浅色光晕）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1215642481162887168","date":"2020-01-10","text":"Ok I went ahead and put this whole project on water. Long time fans of the show know this was inevitable.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/world/townDemo.js","note":"整个项目放到水上：小镇场景就是水上码头","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1212732478458343424","date":"2020-01-02","text":"Added some flags. Gotta make it homely and welcoming.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"每个建筑体量最高的屋脊点（≥3 层，约一半）插杆挂旗；旗面 6×3 细分，顶点着色器沿旗面传播正弦波，朝向顺风","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1210969316071477248","date":"2019-12-28","text":"I've got mom and dad visiting. They've been alternating admiring their new grandchild and building this little town","topic":"build","status":"na","where":"","note":"爸妈来访搭小镇，无技术内容","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1209519206233968641","date":"2019-12-24","text":"A very merry Christmas to you all","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1205422438437273601","date":"2019-12-13","text":"For doors and windows, I use som stencil buffer shenanigans to punch holes in the zbuffer. I admit it was a bit fiddly to figure out.","topic":"build","status":"ref","where":"","note":"用模板缓冲在 z-buffer 上给门窗挖洞；我们的门窗是贴在墙外的几何，不需要挖洞","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1205420678859632640","date":"2019-12-13","text":"For the plants, I dug up this ol' trick: alpha is view angle modulated by leaf texture mapped to a sphere.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"rim = 1-|N·V|，叶片噪声贴在植物自己的坐标上；rim 超过阈值镂空，阈值附近一圈画墨色 → 叶状毛边 + 贴合墨线（替代反向外壳）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1205416648397721601","date":"2019-12-13","text":"New prop placement system! It tries to place as many props as it can without overlap. I use it for doors and windows too, which means they are no longer skewed when placed on skewed tiles, which means skewed tiles now look less awkward.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js（tryPlace）","note":"门窗按道具放置：尽量多放、互不重叠，开口不随格子歪斜","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1201179450668441600","date":"2019-12-01","text":"Icons!","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"ui.html（图标）","note":"粗黑描边白图形 + 彩色圆角底；选中项歪一点、放大、白色小三角","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1200520827898343425","date":"2019-11-29","text":"DnD hopefulls needn't fear no more, for I've now made the backend of letting you tune your town to your favorite palette.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/core/palette.js · 工具栏调色板按钮","note":"调色板后端：小镇 / 粉彩 / 暮色三套墙色，一键切换（画面：彩色小镇逐步变灰再换色）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1198957499027795969","date":"2019-11-25","text":"That bit of text up top is the save data for the current construction. I think I've packed the data about as tight as I can. Keeping the save data in a string will make constructions easily shareable between platforms (when it comes to that)","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"src/world/save.js · app.js","note":"存档=字符串，可分享（原有，版本升到 v4 以适配新网格）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1197909675443916803","date":"2019-11-22","text":"Turns out my monitor was too saturated, making me make my colors too dull. This should be better. I've also added some building effects, grass in the gardens, and colored \"bounce\" \"lighting\". I'm real happy even my yellows look good now. Yellows are hard","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"彩色\"反弹光\"（AO 栅格里同时存墙色）、花园草地；屋顶统一陶土色、墙才是调色板颜色","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1195463004919357443","date":"2019-11-15","text":"My brother @mast4461 had a go. Being an engineer he obviously built a nice fractal. Bonus points if you can name it","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1191990107785572352","date":"2019-11-06","text":"Ah, the timeless problem of shrubbery that look good from all angles without too much overdraw. Adding an anchored center vert to the billboards makes them a bit less flat and gives them directionality without messing with the rotation","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js（tuftGeometry 的 aCenter）","note":"广告牌加锚定中心点：四个三角围着中心点，中心往镜头推，卡片鼓起来有朝向感，又不影响旋转","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1190191289922465793","date":"2019-11-01","text":"Trying out some per vertex voxel based shadows. Not great not terrible. Looks better when not moving, and with less contrast, obviously.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（computeVoxelShadows / aVox）","note":"逐顶点体素阴影：顶点朝太阳在体素里走，被挡就压暗直射光；面板「体素阴影」（和作者结论一样：不好不坏）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1189908238566903808","date":"2019-10-31","text":"However, if you are more careful in providing structural support you'll get curvy brick arches instead and you can build these neat airy cathedral structures","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"两侧（对边）都有支撑时变成拱：半圆拱腹 + 拱肩墙，墙色","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1189902695303458816","date":"2019-10-31","text":"It was real fun making the steel beam support structures. They have this neat artificial yet organic feel to them. Its a place where the WFC algorithm really shines and that would be hard or at least laborious to create with other systems.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"悬空方块下长深色钢架：角柱 + 横梁 + 斜撑，立在水里的腿有泡沫圈","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1189109278361165825","date":"2019-10-29","text":"I'm happy to announce that at a count of 378 I've now built enough modules to cover all possible cases in whatever funky townscape you might want to build with this.","topic":"build","status":"ref","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"378 个模块覆盖所有情况——确认了\"按角点组合查模块\"的思路，本实现用规则生成几何代替手工模块","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1181464374839521280","date":"2019-10-08","text":"I made some stairs, plus an additional smaller WFC for surface decorations like windows and doors (who's awkward placement otherwise explodes the permutation count) I'll give my first talk on this at Indicade in Paris on the 19th. Hope to see you there! https:// indiecade-europe.eu/en/programme/c onferences …","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js · src/world/navlayer.js","note":"楼梯放在导航图用到的崖脚；门窗另起一层小 WFC：每栋每层一种窗型、一扇门","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1178731576982724611","date":"2019-09-30","text":"I made some grassy plots. I'm real happy with the shapes they make. Eventually, they'll grow some trees and the like.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js（后院）","note":"草地块（后院草坪）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1176516621223043073","date":"2019-09-24","text":"Getting a feel for the style and density of windows. Here you can also see what I'm going for when different colors meet","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"窗户的风格与密度（每层 1–2 扇白框小窗）、不同颜色的房子相接","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1174406613031170049","date":"2019-09-18","text":"Today my good friend @podzimcore became the first outsider to take the new project for a spin. Behold the glorious monstrosity he constructed","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1168571866405097472","date":"2019-09-02","text":"A peek at my ambient occlusion approach. The occlusion lives in a layered mesh that's reprojected to a texture at each change. That texture is then blurred, and sampled in the vertex shader of whatever needs lighting.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/bake.js","note":"分层遮蔽：每层一张占用栅格 → 盒式模糊两遍 → 每个顶点沿法线外移采样","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1168168400155267072","date":"2019-09-01","text":"Got some very basic lighting in there. Since this ain't proper voxels I had to do a new take on my usual voxel based AO approach","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/light/bake.js","note":"很基础的光照 + 非真体素的 AO 新做法（画面：灰色城墙模型），即分层 AO 烘焙","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1164926304640229376","date":"2019-08-23","text":"WFC running at interactive speed on that funky grid. Next up is to make it deterministic","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"","note":"不规则网格上交互速度的 WFC（白色城堡）。重构版用规则装配，没上 WFC","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1163836000688365571","date":"2019-08-20","text":"Basic marching cubes on my funky grid. Next up is turning this into mixed initiative WFC.","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"在不规则网格上做 Marching Cubes（红色块）。重构版的建筑是按邻居装配的体素列，思路同源","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1151770831619534848","date":"2019-07-18","text":"I figured out how to make do with relaxation clusters of 3 instead of 7, which means I have to generate fewer unrelaxed patches before I can start relaxing, which makes it faster. Note also that the black and the white grid are *dual* to each other. This is an important concept","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/infinite.js · grids.html","note":"3 块一簇松弛；黑白两张网格互为对偶","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1151152046055272449","date":"2019-07-16","text":"Having a look around","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1151137783785771008","date":"2019-07-16","text":"As promised: an aperiodic infinite deterministic irregular relaxed quadrilateral grid.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/infinite.js · grids.html","note":"无限、确定、无缝的松弛四边形网格：一块块六边形冒出来","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1147881669350891521","date":"2019-07-07","text":"I present: Fairly even irregular quads grid in a hex Todo: 1. Heuristic to reduce (or eliminate) 6 quad verts 2. Tile these babies to infinity","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/grid.js","note":"三角形六边形 → 随机两两合并成菱形 → 三角形切 3 格、菱形切 4 格 → 逐格求最佳正方形并松弛。替换了原来\"六边形切 6 个风筝块 + 抖动\"的错误做法","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1120036868966502401","date":"2019-04-21","text":"It's marching squares on irregular quadrilateral grids","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/world.js","note":"不规则四边形上的 marching squares：角点取值决定模块，作为后续模块化的参考","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1105131621391495176","date":"2019-03-11","text":"Squiggly distance fields, now with animation! Versatile, flexible, but quite laborious","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"textures.html（扭动距离场 → 镜像纹饰 + 展开动画）","note":"镜像 UV 上的对称纹饰距离场，用从中心长出的半径做阈值动画，再叠扭动","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1104771432440049664","date":"2019-03-10","text":"Squiggly distance fields on mirrored UVs for fast and easy UI decorations. Distance field cutoff can be tweaked separately for borders and center. All one texture, just flipped around a bit. At the start of making @BadNorthGame , UI decoration was a pain, it is now a delight.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（扭动距离场）","note":"UI 形状存成距离场，采样前用 6fps 逐格变化的噪声扭坐标 → 手绘抖动；同一个场取不同阈值 = 填充 / 描边 / 内线 / 外发光","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1097458505315946496","date":"2019-02-18","text":"The Viking frontier in @BadNorthGame is dripping with funky math: 1. Triangulate (with some added padding) 2. Walk on triangle edges along each frontier step 3. Bezier sample 4. Tessellate the fields on either side using the bezier and the triangulation","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/generate.js","note":"1 岛屿高度场（扭曲 fbm + 脊线 + 径向衰减）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1092709665199345664","date":"2019-02-05","text":"k-pow !!","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1078792665980915714","date":"2018-12-28","text":"friday night campaign map node graffing","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/campaign/campaign.js（Delaunay 邻接）+ campaign.html 第 2 步","note":"战役节点之间的连线改用 Delaunay 三角网（去掉过长边 + 补最近 2 邻），画面上半那张白色三角网","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1063115611289645057","date":"2018-11-15","text":"Like many of you have suggested, I finally added grass to slopes to make navigability easier to read (especially on overcast levels where the lighting ain't helping much). I'm happy enough with the result to ditch the previous white dotted lines. https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North/ …","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"坡面（邻居高度不同的顶面）草丛密度是平地的 2 倍多","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1062374549407350790","date":"2018-11-13","text":"To make Bad North even prettier, I'm adding some extra smoothing to the island using my voxel normals. It helps break up the grid and make it all look a wee bit more natural. (also, go wishlist @BadNorthGame on Steam: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North/ … )","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/meshwriter.js","note":"Bad North 用体素法线做额外平滑：这里软三角形在同一位置按夹角(<55°)平均法线 → 弯崖壁圆润、崖顶边仍硬","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1061229717582475264","date":"2018-11-10","text":"But you can break up that repetition by using a few different ones with different settings (all still using the same texture)","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（UI 装饰）","note":"同一张装饰贴图的几种不同设置打破重复","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1061227418961219585","date":"2018-11-10","text":"Obviously, if you stretch it too far, you will start to notice the repetition","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"textures.html（UI 装饰 → 只镜像）","note":"拉太长会看出重复：「只镜像」模式下能看到，后两个模式用 8 向与多种设置打破","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1061221291137605633","date":"2018-11-10","text":"I'm writing a simple graphic for UI decoration. A single texture can be oriented 8 different ways and mirrors around the center to work in any size. (also, Bad North drops on Steam Nov 16 https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North/ … )","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（UI 装饰）","note":"一张贴图 8 种朝向 + 以中心镜像，任意尺寸都能用","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1056999668486471682","date":"2018-10-29","text":"Works well in daylight too, largely thanks to the max blend","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js（MaxEquation）","note":"白天也好看的火：靠 Max 混合，粒子融成一个火焰轮廓不过曝（北境里小屋失守时着火）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1056992291108413446","date":"2018-10-29","text":"Oh no! I made an error! The quads above shrink way more than they are supposed to. This looks much better and breaks up the flame in a much more interesting way:","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js（fsize）","note":"火的面片往上缩得比\"应该的\"快得多（(1-age)²），火焰顶端碎成小块","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1056990611738451968","date":"2018-10-29","text":"New fire effect. For blend mode, I use Max instead of Add to have better control over my colors and to make the particles blend together and form a common silhouette.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js","note":"烟囱口发射软圆粒子，黄 → 橙 → 红；混合方程 MaxEquation：重叠处取最大值而不是相加 → 融成一个轮廓、白天也不发白（1056999668486471682）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1042732450730913793","date":"2018-09-20","text":"The graph generator I ended up using for the Bad North campaign maps: 1. Create nodes of varying sizes and spread them out 2. Cull nodes outside bounds 3. Do a random walk from start to finish 4. Do some more random walks 5. Pick some more random nodes","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/campaign/campaign.js · campaign.html","note":"战役图：节点散开 → 剔除 → 起终点随机游走 → 再走几条 → 再挑节点","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1024679338292256769","date":"2018-08-01","text":"Some UI flair","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"textures.html（扭动距离场 → 镜像纹饰 + 展开动画）","note":"\"Ring of Command\" 那种对称纹饰从中心展开、停、收回","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1022855252574437376","date":"2018-07-27","text":"it's my birthday!","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1022573208590057472","date":"2018-07-26","text":"The look and feel of the basic meat and potato melee combat is one of the things I'm most proud of in Bad North","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（#hit）","note":"近战手感：挨打后退一步、喷血滴（抛物线落地）、受伤越重身上越红","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1017355723171344385","date":"2018-07-12","text":"Making some thicker outlines for all you 4k high ballers out there","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/outline.js（thickness）","note":"更粗的描边：线宽按像素比 × 分辨率（以 1080 高为基准）放大；面板「粗描边」再翻倍","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1016680972610359298","date":"2018-07-10","text":"This is what the confirm popup looks like:","topic":"tools","status":"done","where":"ui.html（确认弹出）","note":"点小队 → 选择 / 移动 / 交换三个按钮沿圆弧依次弹出（超调弹簧缓动），再点收回","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015151731804721152","date":"2018-07-06","text":"I change the mip level of the noise texture throughout the smoke trail. This aids the transition from crisp at the base to blurry a the tip","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/life/smoke.js（mip 偏移 = aAge×4）","note":"沿烟的轨迹提高噪声的 mip 级别：底部清晰、顶端模糊","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015149712469524480","date":"2018-07-06","text":"I only sample my noise texture once per quad, but I scroll the UVs randomly forward or backward along the flow of the smoke. This further breaks up the recognizability of individual blobs and it creates some of that cool multi layered flow feeling thick smoke should have","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/life/smoke.js（aDir）","note":"每片只采样一次噪声，UV 沿烟的流向随机前 / 后滚；面板「烟·棋盘格调试」可看（画面就是棋盘格）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015142746372366336","date":"2018-07-06","text":"I solve the problems of z-depth and draw order by drawing the effect in 2 passes. The first pass is black, and and has a full alpha ner the base. The second pass is lighter, more transparent towards the base, and has its cutoff pulled in 1 pixel (creating the crisp outline)","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/life/smoke.js（PASS 0 / 1）","note":"两遍画：第一遍黑、底部 alpha 满；第二遍浅、底部更透明、阈值往里收 1 像素（fwidth）→ 黑描边","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015140880666300416","date":"2018-07-06","text":"Smoke effect. A full billowy base tied together by a crisp outline seamlessly transitioned to a blurry fade. The effect is probably a bit much for my current purposes, but I think it solves some interesting problems so I wanted to share it","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/life/smoke.js","note":"浓烟：底部饱满翻滚 + 清楚的轮廓，往上过渡成模糊淡出（北境小屋失守时冒黑烟）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1010979395719319552","date":"2018-06-24","text":"A selection of the many handsome faces you might come across in @BadNorthGame","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"ui.html（头像生成器下排）","note":"游戏内头像：切角方框、红蓝背景、肩膀与人群剪影、尖盔护鼻","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587828992266240","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587825024425984","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587821220229120","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587817021636609","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587812462530561","date":"2018-06-15","text":"Proper games have waterfalls. I'm glad to report that @BadNorthGame is now a proper game.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/water/waterfall.js","note":"瀑布：河从崖边落下的白色水帘 + 底部白沫（面板「瀑布」）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"999191760944418817","date":"2018-05-23","text":"Adding the option of disabling gore made me realized just how much I rely on blood for environmental storytelling. I should probably start asking some questions about what kind of person I am and what kind of art I put into this world.","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（gore）","note":"关掉血腥：面板「血腥」取消勾选后不画血、不留尸体（画面就是同一场战斗的有血 / 无血对比）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"999185422403055616","date":"2018-05-23","text":"For my blood splatter UVs, I'm interpolating between sprite-space and skin-space using the fwidth of skin UV. This gives me a sprite-space map on the tummy (where the skin UVs are static) while the splatter on the face follows the actual motion of the head.","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（aSoak · onBeforeCompile）","note":"血迹跟着身体：血斑按物体空间坐标的噪声画，所以随身体动；血量越少斑越多。原作是精灵空间和皮肤空间按 fwidth 插值（我们是 3D 小人，直接用物体空间）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"995043346778415104","date":"2018-05-11","text":"The pathfinding in some levels does get a bit convoluted","topic":"fx","status":"ref","where":"src/world/navgraph.js","note":"有些关卡寻路很绕（画面：小队在多层台地、洞口之间绕路）。重构版寻路走导航图，没有洞穴里的路","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"995034777756536833","date":"2018-05-11","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"987267068495003648","date":"2018-04-20","text":"Using inspector expressions, I can live tweak the cost function of my projectile trajectory lookup tables. Very handy.","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（LUT / lookupShot）","note":"弹道查找表 + 代价函数：按 (距离, 高差) 预先找代价最小的出射角（飞行时间 + 落角偏离 45°），箭按真抛物线飞","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"984813819280191488","date":"2018-04-13","text":"Blood soaking as a health indicator for the big fellas and a proper stun state for the little ones","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（soak）","note":"血浸透当血量指示：受伤的单位身上红色越来越多","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"984703192465330176","date":"2018-04-13","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"978211952504852480","date":"2018-03-26","text":"Pro tip: use fwidth, ddx and ddy to create crisp, pixel perfect, zoom independent, antialiased lines with your shaders. https:// computergraphics.stackexchange.com/questions/61/w hat-is-fwidth-and-how-does-it-work …","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"textures.html（抗锯齿线）","note":"fwidth 画与缩放无关的 1 像素抗锯齿线；左右对比固定宽度 step（远处断、近处粗）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"978195201901711360","date":"2018-03-26","text":"Some of it will have to wait for some later project","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"978194866520944641","date":"2018-03-26","text":"Some of it looks very similar","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"974579499802202113","date":"2018-03-16","text":"For a given position, Barycentric Coordinates can be calculated with 1 subtraction and 1 dot product (if you've precalculated some nice vectors in the triangle)","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/spatial.js（baryPrep）","note":"重心坐标：预先算两个对偶向量，之后每个坐标 1 次减法 + 1 次点积","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"974564862729838592","date":"2018-03-16","text":"I'm making some pedagogical gizmos for my GDC microtalk, like this illustration of Barycentric Coordinates. Gizmos > powerpoints.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"grids.html（重心坐标）","note":"讲课用的重心坐标小工具：三角形 + 拖动的点 + 三个权重","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"974325184525201409","date":"2018-03-15","text":"We were having strange crashes when using Unity's Physics.OverlapBox. We solved it (hopefully) by making our own box-box test in two incredibly stressful hours. Behold, our beautiful viking raid planner:","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/core/obb.js","note":"自己写的盒-盒测试：分离轴 15 根，平行轴（叉积≈0）跳过；3000 对随机盒与撒点对照，漏判 0，2 次是棱对棱交叉撒点撒不到","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"972829402873716737","date":"2018-03-11","text":"If you're heading to GDC, come see my microtalk about the triangular flow fields we use for pathfinding and combat http:// schedule.gdconf.com/session/tech-t oolbox/854263 …","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/flowfield.js","note":"寻路和战斗用的流场：所有守军同时作源的 Dijkstra，每 0.25 秒一次，查询 O(1)","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"969860566322958336","date":"2018-03-03","text":"My unit sprites have 1 direction, so they need to be directionally ambiguous. They are mostly symmetrical and avoid features that feel jarring when they flip. Would these sword tips be axe heads, you would notice at a glance that they are pointing in two distinct directions","topic":"fx","status":"ref","where":"","note":"单向精灵：士兵只有一个朝向，靠左右翻转，所以造型要对称、翻转不突兀。我们的士兵是 3D 小模型，不需要","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"959752525867036672","date":"2018-02-03","text":"A great unexpected joy in this project has been writing my own navmesh. It's an oddly relaxing job full of small and approachable math-puzzles. Here you see some pulsating vertex cells; a dual to the triangular grid and a suitable place to start with foliage placement.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"grids.html（对偶图）· src/life/vegetation.js","note":"顶点格 = 三角网的对偶，植被落点从这里开始；网格实验室可开「对偶图」","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"959530111187013632","date":"2018-02-02","text":"I've been tweaking the foliage system today. It now supports multiple grass types per level.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"每关多种草；画面里的小花是一大片一大片的白色碎点（已按此重做小花）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"958410200146497537","date":"2018-01-30","text":"The approach is versatile enough that I can use it for the ingame banners too","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"ui.html（旗帜生成器）","note":"同一个生成器换一棵部件树：旗形（尖 / 缺口 / 燕尾 / 方）→ 1–2 个大徽记 + 小点缀","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"958371606350454784","date":"2018-01-30","text":"The beginnings of a portrait generator. It currently runs on 5 examples (all male and with a similar hierarchy) but it's content agnostic and should support a diverse set of inputs.","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"ui.html（头像生成器）","note":"内容无关的层级部件生成器：头 → 耳（镜像）/ 头发 / 眼（镜像）/ 胡子 / 嘴 / 鼻，每槽挑变体 + 尺寸抖动","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"946660607008403456","date":"2017-12-29","text":"While @rtm223 is away on holiday I'm taking some time to focus on the important things, like making blood, corpses and arrows stick to boats and adding pretty little flowers","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js","note":"Bad North 战斗：血、尸体、箭粘在船上随船走（北境场景）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"943230624369868800","date":"2017-12-19","text":"And yeah, obviously the snow flakes are affected by the wind system and thus flow around the island","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/life/atmosphere.js","note":"3000 片雪沿风场平流 + 下落 + 飘摆；落进地面 / 出界从上风边重新生成；开雪时主材质朝上的面混白（台地、屋顶积雪）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"943230620242796544","date":"2017-12-19","text":"I'm heading north for a few days to see the folks. In the meantime, here's some seasonally relevant hype material for @BadNorthGame :","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"938422757288792064","date":"2017-12-06","text":"I'm extra happy with how the grouping turned out. It's a sort of cellular automaton where nodes get eaten by the neighbor group to which they are most connected. Here's a slowmo to illustrate:","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/campaign/campaign.js（groupRegions）","note":"分组元胞自动机：每次挑最小的组，整组并进和它连边最多的邻组，直到剩 6 组（战役图第 4 步的颜色）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"938405900573986816","date":"2017-12-06","text":"A more legible peek at the campaign generation for @BadNorthGame . Islands get spread apart and divided into regions.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/campaign/campaign.js","note":"战役图节点分成几片彩色区域，竖长条，上起点下终点","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"938395867215728640","date":"2017-12-06","text":"Node graph programming is by far the most delightful programming","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"","note":"节点图编程（画面：一长条彩色节点图编辑器）。没有可搬的技术","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"931196707236392960","date":"2017-11-16","text":"My generated levels all keep a virtual voxel space. It is used for light baking, soft normals, various 3D textures, simplified collision, wind simulation etc.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/core/world.js","note":"虚拟体素空间：World 的 solid / rock 位，同时用于光照烘焙、软法线、风场、体素阴影、碰撞（岛的体素块画面）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"929417420921556993","date":"2017-11-11","text":"Fun fact: I generate smooth normals for all my meshes and use a blend between smooth and hard normals in the final lighting","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/view.js（uNormMix）","note":"平滑 / 硬法线在最终光照里混合：硬法线由屏幕空间导数算，和平滑法线按 0.8 混（面板「软硬法线混合」）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"926903893866541057","date":"2017-11-04","text":"Here is what my wind vectors look like. They can be used by all kinds of systems, including shaders","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/life/atmosphere.js","note":"每层一张 2D 网格：实心格栅格化再模糊 = 阻挡度 b；风 = 基础风向去掉\"撞向障碍物\"的法向分量（贴边只剩切向）、贴边加速、被挡住往上抬；sample(x,y,z) 三线性；面板「风场箭头」显示两层箭头","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"926890207298899969","date":"2017-11-04","text":"Not really. I build a custom mesh for the flag using a bezier curve along virtual wind particles","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（#flag / #updateFlag）","note":"军旗 = 沿虚拟风粒子的贝塞尔曲线自己生成的网格：旗杆顶放出 3 个粒子，跟着前一个走、被风吹；小队走动时旗子拖在后面","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"926834721392340992","date":"2017-11-04","text":"The banners where due for a makeover. I built a wind system to get them flapping just right","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（#updateFlag）· life/atmosphere.js","note":"军旗翻新：风取共享风场在旗杆顶的值 + 阵风，贝塞尔旗面；画面里地图上是风场格点","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"917405214638006273","date":"2017-10-09","text":"A somewhat major breakthrough in my procedural generation: a heuristic for deliberately generating navigable levels","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/island.js","note":"生成可走关卡的启发式：生成后用导航图检查每块台地能否从沙滩走上去，走不到的削低一档（画面：黄色可走连线）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"913407568730615808","date":"2017-09-28","text":"Ok, I'm proud of this one. Can any of you brainy nerds figure out what we're looking at here?","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"912691357440978945","date":"2017-09-26","text":"Long time no combat gifs","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（#hit）","note":"战斗动图：台地边上混战、血、落水的人；挨打后退 + 血滴飞溅落地成血点","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"911913981731885056","date":"2017-09-24","text":"I'm looking at the campaign map. Saving island snapshots to 64² textures and then crisping them back up with some shader magic","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/campaign/campaign.js（islandSnapshot）","note":"战役图上的岛：存成 64² 小图，放大时阈值收脆，点线相连","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"906425294533394432","date":"2017-09-09","text":"It's like navigating a Swiss cheese","topic":"fx","status":"partial","where":"src/world/layerednav.js · navigation.html","note":"本轮逐帧复核246帧：新增 world/layerednav.js，直接从共享 World 枚举洞底/洞顶多层节点，净空与台阶验证，navigation.html 可对照柱顶假设。北境战斗完整多层接入仍待补齐。","project":"badnorth","learned":"本轮逐帧复核246帧：新增 world/layerednav.js，直接从共享 World 枚举洞底/洞顶多层节点，净空与台阶验证，navigation.html 可对照柱顶假设。北境战斗完整多层接入仍待补齐。","reviewEvidence":"artifacts/coverage/navigation-review.md","decodedFrames":246},{"id":"906416813810049025","date":"2017-09-09","text":"New cave tileset. These levels really challenge your spacial skills #screenshotsaturday #madewithunity @BadNorthGame","topic":"fx","status":"partial","where":"src/terrain/features.js","note":"新的洞窟图块：岩体里有拱洞、单位从洞里穿过；重构版只有造型，导航不走洞","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"906207980802252801","date":"2017-09-08","text":"I've been working on some new fog (sped up in the gif). For background effects, subtlety is key.","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/life/atmosphere.js","note":"岛周围一张大圆盘，alpha 随半径 smoothstep 增大、叠两层缓慢流动的噪声，颜色取背景色偏白 —— 背景效果，宁淡勿浓","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"903647529203634176","date":"2017-09-01","text":"Spears are so weird to implement. I can see why most games don't use them","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（pike）","note":"长矛：第二队守军是矛兵，够得更远（0.44 vs 0.28）先出手；画面里矛兵在滩上列阵","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"902103473365417984","date":"2017-08-28","text":"Ok, one more visualization. Distances this time. I really should get back to proper work now","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"902069261304287232","date":"2017-08-28","text":"Just for fun: visualization of data inheritance in my flow/distance/influence fields","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/flowfield.js · battle.js（#drawFlow）","note":"数据继承可视化：每格到父格一段线，颜色 = 从哪支守军继承来的（面板「流场」）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"901842167508992000","date":"2017-08-27","text":"Made my flow/influence fields even smarter: In addition to distance and direction to nearest unit, it can now tell you what type they are","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/flowfield.js","note":"流场 / 影响场：除了到最近单位的距离和方向，还带着\"那是什么兵种\"；维京人看到矛兵正面会绕开去打小屋","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"901469409579061248","date":"2017-08-26","text":"Working on nicer ship wakes","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/life/boats.js · src/badnorth/battle.js","note":"长船尾迹：船尾两道向外张开的白线 / 白点，越远越淡","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"880853661936734211","date":"2017-06-30","text":"Units got stuck when meeting in narrow passages. I fixed it by introducing left handed traffic. Never felt so clever.","topic":"fx","status":"partial","where":"src/world/traffic.js · src/badnorth/battle.js","note":"本轮逐帧复核601帧：原横向偏移为0，现新增窄道识别与确定左侧目标，并限制偏移在多边形内部；战斗已接入，测试相反方向车道。点线标示与拥挤压力测试仍待补齐。","project":"badnorth","learned":"本轮逐帧复核601帧：原横向偏移为0，现新增窄道识别与确定左侧目标，并限制偏移在多边形内部；战斗已接入，测试相反方向车道。点线标示与拥挤压力测试仍待补齐。","reviewEvidence":"artifacts/coverage/navigation-review.md","decodedFrames":601},{"id":"877995885250138119","date":"2017-06-22","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"870558914345041921","date":"2017-06-02","text":"I think we've all had days like this","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"870296307889573889","date":"2017-06-01","text":"Units can now get knocked off ledges","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/badnorth/battle.js（#hit / #fallStep）","note":"单位会被打下悬崖：挨打时身后低 ≥2 层就可能被击飞，抛物线落下，落差大的摔死","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"797119718477991936","date":"2016-11-11","text":"Got some basic navigation going","topic":"fx","project":"badnorth","status":"partial","where":"src/world/layerednav.js · navigation.html","note":"本轮逐帧复核265帧：模块生成后内部多层活动点。新增共享 World 多层导航与门户边；混合格和四边形测试通过。预制模块精细内部 portal 与战斗接入仍待补齐。","learned":"本轮逐帧复核265帧：模块生成后内部多层活动点。新增共享 World 多层导航与门户边；混合格和四边形测试通过。预制模块精细内部 portal 与战斗接入仍待补齐。","reviewEvidence":"artifacts/coverage/navigation-review.md","decodedFrames":265}]};
